[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read one report at a time,
the ticket holds more than one bug. The desk merged on subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and the subjects are the same for every
problem below: "wrong day", "dates mixed up". The bodies are not.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row. The other problems keep coming in after it ships.
</Callout>

## One row per problem

Counted from the ticket export at render time. Each report sits in exactly one row. Reports are
placed by their tenant (locale and booking form, `causes.ts`), not by the intake tag, which is a
guess from the reporter's browser.

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: { label: 'ai-training#1', href: 'https://github.com/rogasoft/ai-training/issues/1' },
    hint: { label: 'ai-training#2', href: 'https://github.com/rogasoft/ai-training/issues/2' },
    'one-day': { label: 'ai-training#3', href: 'https://github.com/rogasoft/ai-training/issues/3' },
  }}
/>

## The problems

**`parser`: day and month swap.** The shared parser reads every date month first. All our tenants
on file write the day first, so 7 April becomes 4 July. Where a report in this row names both
dates, they are the same day and month, swapped. This is the bug #4471 was opened for, and the fix queued
for it.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first.** Tenants on `booking-v3` show
`MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type what the hint says, and the form reads the
date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not touch this. The form's hint has to
follow the tenant's locale. Only reports sent through the form of a `booking-v3` tenant are in
this row; the same tenants' app and email reports are parser reports.

**`one-day`: the date moves by a day, it does not swap.** These reports describe a date that is
one day early or late, a meeting that lands on different days for people in different cities, and
an invite that arrives before the booking was made. No day and month are swapped. This reads as a
time zone or day-boundary bug in how invites are built. The desk had noted these reports
(`desk-notes.json`) but counted them under `parser`. The parser fix will not change them.

## What to do on the desk

- Point new reports at the row they match, not at #4471 by subject.
- When the parser fix ships, keep #4471's count to its own row. A report about the form hint or a
  one-day move is not "still broken after the fix"; it is a different ticket.
- Matching on subject merged three bugs into one count. Read the body before you merge.

